1:1 COMMENT "# forbind.z -- counting loops."
1:31 EOL "\n"
2:1 COMMENT "#"
2:2 EOL "\n"
3:1 COMMENT "# A `for` binding names an ITERATOR, so a counted loop is written with the"
3:75 EOL "\n"
4:1 COMMENT "# range members and the compiler owns the counter: `n.each` for a half-open"
4:76 EOL "\n"
5:1 COMMENT "# count, `a.upto to: b` for a closed one. There is no C-style header binding --"
5:80 EOL "\n"
6:1 COMMENT "# `for i: 0 while i < n loop { i = i + 1 }` is refused, because a binding that"
6:79 EOL "\n"
7:1 COMMENT "# is not an iterator has nothing to yield."
7:43 EOL "\n"
8:1 COMMENT "#"
8:2 EOL "\n"
9:1 COMMENT "# A loop that must control its own step writes the counter as an ordinary local"
9:80 EOL "\n"
10:1 COMMENT "# and tests it in the header, which is what `stepby` does below."
10:65 EOL "\n"
11:1 EOL "\n"
